==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|uwila|ūwila|lang=goh}}, from a variant of {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|uwwalǭ|lang=gem-pro}} (compare Dutch {{term|uil|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|ûle|lang=fy}}, English {{term|owl|lang=en}}), diminutive of {{recons|uwwǭ|lang=gem-pro}} ‘eagle-owl’ (compare German {{term|Uhu|lang=de}}), of imitative origin or a variant of {{recons|ūfaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|ūfǭ|lang=gem-pro}} (compare Swedish {{term|uv|lang=sv}} ‘horned owl’, Bavarian {{term|Auf|lang=bav}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|up-|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʔɔɪ̯lə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Eulen}}

# [[owl]]
# a [[moth]] of the family [[Noctuidae]]

